[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read by cause, it holds three problems that need
three different fixes. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Fixing the parser leaves the form reports and the one-day reports wrong.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="JakSko/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }} />

## How to tell them apart

- **Parser** ([ticket](https://github.com/JakSko/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)): a day-first
  tenant's date is read month first, so day and month trade places. Any channel: app, email, and
  the form on tenants that do not run booking-v3.
- **Form hint** ([ticket](https://github.com/JakSko/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)): booking-v3
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, and people type what it says. Only through the form,
  only on booking-v3 tenants. The bodies read like parser reports; the channel and the form tell
  them apart.
- **One day early** ([ticket](https://github.com/JakSko/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3)): the
  weekday is off by one, or two time zones see two days. No day and month swap. The desk already
  had these as one-day moves in `desk-notes.json`.

## How this was counted

Every report in `reports-4471.json`, once per id (the export pages overlap). The cause comes from
the tenant's locale, booking form and channel (`causes.ts`), not from the subject line or the intake
tag; the desk's one-day moves are taken out as their own problem. Then the bodies were read: each
names a booked date and a shown date that fit its problem. One report on the one-day list has no
dates; it stays there on the desk's reading.

## Data

Built from the export of 2026-10-04 (`src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`) at render time. If the desk
merges more reports into #4471, the table changes with them; each ticket keeps the count of the day
it was filed.

